-- title:
--   Strict first-kind places: unramified over α and unique
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a natural number $N \neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$. Let `data` consist of a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ vanishing on the pair $(j, j_q)$, let `hKr` assert that its reduction mod $q$ is $(\mathbf{C}X^q - X)(\mathbf{C}X - X^q)$, and let $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ assert that the two degeneracy embeddings $\alpha =$ `heckeAlphaBar` and $\beta =$ `heckeBetaBar` of the level-$N$ Laurent-series field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-field into the level-$Nq$ one are integral ring homomorphisms. Let $P$ be a place specialisation for these data, $R$ a prolongation tuple over $P$, $v$ a place of $k$-field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ generated by the reductions of $j$ and $j_N$, and $S$ a set of functions at level $Nq$. Assume $q \nmid N$ and that `IsChartAt R v S` holds, i.e. $S$ is a chart at $v$ for $R$: its members are integral for the first regular prolongation and their residues are regular at $v$, $S$ contains the prescribed generators (in the affine or in the cuspidal case), contains the constants from $A$, satisfies a denominator clause, a value law relating values at places of the first kind to their reductions at $v$, a separation clause for places of the second kind, an étale clause, the dichotomy that every place reducing to $v$ is strict of the first or of the second kind, and regularity of members of $S$ at all places reducing to $v$; these clauses are summarised here. Finally let $W$ be a place of the level-$Nq$ field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which is strict of the first kind for $P$ (the geometric Frobenius on level-$N$ places carries $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,W$ to $P.\mathrm{reduceSnd}\,W$, and its square does not fix $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,W$), with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,W = v$, where $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,W$ is the specialisation under $P.\mathrm{sp}$ of the restriction of $W$ along $\alpha$. The conclusion is twofold: the ramification index of $W$ over its restriction along $\alpha$ equals $1$, and any place $W'$ of the level-$Nq$ field which is strict of the first kind and satisfies $W'|_{\alpha} = W|_{\alpha}$ equals $W$.
--
--   This is the local statement, at a place strict of the first kind, that the first degeneracy map $X_0(Nq) \to X_0(N)$ is unramified at $W$ and injective on the fibre through $W$; it is the first-kind half of the comparison of fibres used in the local semicontinuity analysis of the Kronecker-congruence model. It is used by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.localSemicontinuityFst_of_reducesDivisors_of_hasCoordinates_of_hasCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.localSemicontinuityFst_of_reducesDivisors_of_hasCoordinates_of_hasCharts).
